```gitignore
# Compiled and binary files
*.class
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.a
*.out

# Dependencies
lib/
libs/
dependency/
dependencies/

# Build artifacts
target/
build/
dist/
out/

# IDE files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs and temporary files
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp

# Environment
.env
.env.local
*.env.*

# Coverage and testing
coverage/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Compressed files
*.zip
*.gz
*.tar
*.tgz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.7z
*.rar
*.zst
*.lz4
*.lzh
*.cab
*.arj
*.rpm
*.deb
*.Z
*.lz
*.lzo
*.tar.gz
*.tar.bz2
*.tar.xz
*.tar.zst
```
/run/
/.gradle/

# Working artwork: the generator scripts, their trace cache and every size they
# render are the author's own and are not what the build reads.
#
# The exception is the one picture the jar is built from. It has to be in the
# repository or a build that is not this machine — the release workflow, anybody who
# clones this — produces a jar with no icon in it, silently: the copy below finds no
# file and there is nothing to fail on. The directory's *contents* are excluded rather
# than the directory itself, because a file cannot be brought back once its parent is.
/art/*
!/art/title.png
/store
